## Why This Is Asked
This question probes understanding of per-tenant isolation, backpressure, and queueing strategies under load, a common real-world challenge in llm-ops gateways.

## Key Concepts
- Priority queues and scheduling (WFQ, weighted RR)
- Backpressure and saturation handling
- Tenant isolation and SLA guarantees
- Observability: latency, tail latency, fairness

## Code Example
```javascript
class Scheduler {
  constructor() {
    this.queues = {Gold: [], Silver: [], Bronze: []};
  }
  enqueue(tenant, priority, job) {
    this.queues[priority].push({tenant, job});
  }
  dequeue() {
    for (const p of ['Gold','Silver','Bronze']) {
      if (this.queues[p].length) return this.queues[p].shift();
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and ensure Gold latency bounds under burst?
- How would you adapt weights if Bronze saturates frequently?

## Why This Is Asked
Governance and trust gaps exist in multi-tenant LLM-ops. Provenance and attribution are critical for audits, compliance, and drift detection across tenants.

## Key Concepts
- Data provenance, model attribution, tamper-evident logging, append-only storage
- Per-tenant data contracts and data locality requirements
- Merkle proofs, cryptographic hashing, replayability

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
function logEvent(event){
  const rec = JSON.stringify(event);
  const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(rec).digest('hex');
  appendToWormStore({ ...event, hash, ts: Date.now() });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale the provenance store to 10M events/day?
- How do you enforce tamper-evidence across regional replicas?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates ability to translate privacy and safety requirements into a concrete, low-overhead component that precedes LLM calls and manages per-tenant policy enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant policy surface and versioning
- Lightweight, rule-based prompt classification
- Redaction of PII and disallowed content
- Caching decisions to minimize latency and repeated processing

## Code Example
```javascript
function classifyPrompt(prompt) {
  const p = prompt.toLowerCase();
  if (/ssn|credit card|password/.test(p)) return 'PII';
  if (p.includes('invoice') || p.includes('order')) return 'TRANSACTION';
  return 'GENERAL';
}
```

